import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---
<Layout title="Pied Piper privacy" description="How the local Pied Piper application handles data.">
<article class="container" style="padding-block: 80px; max-width: 800px">
<h1 class="display">Your workspace, your data.</h1>
<p>Pied Piper does not collect product analytics, generate analytics identities, sample process activity for telemetry, or export diagnostic traces, metrics, or logs. Telemetry environment variables and saved exporter settings cannot turn collection back on.</p>
<h2>Local data</h2><p>Projects, conversation history, settings, and operational logs are stored locally. Features you choose to use can read and write files in your workspace.</p>
<h2>Connected services</h2><p>When you connect a coding provider, source-control host, or your own relay, the application communicates with that service to perform your requests. Those services have their own data policies. Removing Pied Piper telemetry does not change the behavior of separately installed provider tools.</p>
<h2>Distribution</h2><p>This source fork does not include the original project's cloud credentials or mobile update feed.</p>
</article></Layout>
